{title: La Cucaracha}
{subtitle: Traditional Mexican Folk Song (Public Domain)}
{artist: Traditional}
{composer: Traditional}
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 120}
{capo: 0}

{comment: This is a traditional public-domain version. 
Many regional variants exist; this one is historically attested.}

{comment: Suggested strumming pattern}
{comment: | D D U U D U |}

{define: G  base-fret 1 frets 3 2 0 0 0 3}
{define: D7 base-fret 1 frets x x 0 2 1 2}
{define: C  base-fret 1 frets x 3 2 0 1 0}

{start_of_chorus}
[G]La cucaracha, [D7]la cucaracha
[G]Ya no puede [D7]caminar
[G]Porque no tiene, [C]porque le falta
[G]Una patita [D7]para andar
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Optional instrumental break}
{comment: | G | D7 | G | D7 | G | C | G D7 | G |}

{start_of_verse}
[G]The little cockroach, [D7]the little cockroach
[G]Now she cannot [D7]walk at all
[G]Because she doesn’t, [C]because she lacks
[G]A little leg to [D7]help her [G]crawl
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
[G]Some say the roach was [D7]very clever
[G]Dancing through the [D7]dusty street
[G]But when she lost her [C]tiny leg
[G]She couldn’t keep up [D7]with the [G]beat
{end_of_verse}

{comment: End with a bright G chord}
